- **Formatting:** Never split simple assignments, ternaries, boolean expressions, or short statements across multiple lines. These must always remain on a single line if they fit within a normal line length.

- **Line breaks:** Do not introduce line breaks for readability in short expressions. Multi-line formatting is only allowed for genuinely long or complex logic.

- **Output rule:** If a statement can fit on one line, it must be on one line.

# Git Workflow Rules

When creating a branch, always follow this naming convention:

Features:
feature/<issue-number>-<short-kebab-case-description>

Bugs:
bug/<issue-number>-<short-kebab-case-description>

Enhancements:
enhancement/<issue-number>-<short-kebab-case-description>

Examples:

feature/42-language-streaks
feature/18-google-auth

bug/73-login-redirect-loop
bug/15-password-reset-failure

enhancement/91-dashboard-performance
enhancement/24-improve-onboarding

Rules:
- Always use lowercase.
- Always use kebab-case.
- Never use spaces.
- Always include the GitHub issue number.
- Never create branches directly from a description without an issue number.